Z||000017||REDHOTT88||12-17-2001||11:03 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B> <BR>Just to clarify... The ONLY input GM had was a lotus car that they LOOKED at when designing the system. Uses a SIMILAR, but completely independantly researched design... How do these rumors get started?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I love my car. It's good to me. Small things break all the time, as to be expected with a 14-year old car. HOWEVER, the parts are STOOPID-Cheap. <P>If you are on ANY form of budget, I would steer away from the 88s. The single model-year run has resulted in parts that are almost impossible to acquire, whereas the 84-87 are DEAD easy. Also, for the money that you'd put into restoring an 88 suspension, you can realistically mod out the 84-87 to be comparable...<P>Other than the suspension differences, the internals haven't changed MUCH over the years. If not abused, and obsessively maintained, the Fiero will be MORE than nice to you. It's an eye-turner. More so if in great condition!<P>Have fun, and ignore the clowns on this forum giving you a hard time... Civility seems somewhat LACKING today   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Maybe I should of said LOTUS "inspired".<P>If I came across as uncivil, I apologize to you.<P>Yes, the 88 was a one time model year, and it can be hard to find parts. But it seems to me this was the actual model Pontiac wanted to make in 84, but lacked the budget... Hence it is that much better of a model, and desirous as a collector car.<P>I plan to own a Fiero from every model year. They are ALL nice cars to ME. ( My 2 cents)<P> <P><P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">       <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> 